Purpose: monomorphic inline caches for get_field, get_field2, put_field and get_var in the QuickJS-ng interpreter (ZN-600), measured
  and NOT applied (D56, docs/reports/zinc-next-qjs-ic.md). Applies on the tree of ZN-599 (patches 0001 and 0002); build with
  -DZN_QJS_IC (CMake: target_compile_definitions(zn_quickjs PRIVATE ZN_QJS_IC)).
Measured: Intel Mac, interpreter with and without, 3 runs: three.js 0.98-1.00x, sprite 0.97-0.98x, objects 1.01-1.06x, matter-js
  0.98-1.02x, with 89-99.9% hits; test262 regexp and the QuickJS T1 programs unchanged; 1.6-5 KB of caches per warmed function.
Upstream: not proposed: upstream removed its inline caches in February 2025 (1.037x average on web-tooling) and closed a monomorphic
  read cache in May 2026 for flat results; these numbers agree.
